    "howto": { "x": 1360, "y": 0, "w": 420, "maxH": 720, "fill": "orange", "size": "m", "text": "How this canvas works\n\n1. One row per Studio template, at Desktop 1280 · Tablet 768 · Phone 390.\n\n2. Change anything. Keep the board names and the spot names (shown in each element's data-spot) so Claude can match your changes back to Studio.\n\n3. Colors and type: use the ClearMark values. Anything off-system is snapped to the nearest ClearMark color, text style or 32px step on the way back, and listed for you.\n\n4. When a template is done: leave a comment on its row starting with READY, e.g. \"READY hero\", and send it to Claude.\n\n5. Claude brings it into Studio. You check it in Design view, then Publish." }
